      ":question/id": "71e6c6e3-bd2d-56df-b5ac-8bd9bdcce5d6",
      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-48039",
      ":question/problem": "Select the function that is continuous at $x =-2$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The correct answer is shown below. Despite the fact that the function has a discontinuity at $x=1$, the graph can be drawn in the neighborhood of $x=-2$ without taking our pencil off of the paper.\n\n![](image_assets/63e7a219c0c9bf7917a094ac0e65e9d4f18eb855476830621700d58ac29ba1b0-63e7a219c0.png)\n\nAll the other given graphs contain breaks at $x=-2$ and it would be impossible to draw them in the neighborhood of $x=-2$ without taking the pencil off of the paper."
    },
